From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:27:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Draw the scene again for a UI only frame of a stereo
 window

F3D redraws the interface over the cached layers of the last frame whenever no
render was requested (the event loop, every input event). The layers hold the last
eye drawn, so in a stereo window the left eye of that frame was the right eye's
picture and both back buffers showed one eye. With two eyes the scene is drawn again.

Found by reading the render framebuffer before VTK's StereoMidpoint blit: it held the
previous frame's right eye, while the same call made without the UI only frames gave
two different eyes.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
 vtkext/private/module/vtkF3DRenderPass.cxx | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vtkext/private/module/vtkF3DRenderPass.cxx b/vtkext/private/module/vtkF3DRenderPass.cxx
index fc72655..be085e9 100644
--- a/vtkext/private/module/vtkF3DRenderPass.cxx
+++ b/vtkext/private/module/vtkF3DRenderPass.cxx
@@ -272,7 +272,10 @@ void vtkF3DRenderPass::Render(const vtkRenderState* s)
 
   vtkRenderer* r = s->GetRenderer();
   vtkInformation* info = r->GetInformation();
-  bool uiOnly = info->Has(vtkF3DRenderPass::RENDER_UI_ONLY());
+  // A UI only frame draws the interface over the layers of the last frame, which hold one eye: with
+  // two eyes the scene is drawn again, so that each eye keeps its own picture
+  bool uiOnly =
+    info->Has(vtkF3DRenderPass::RENDER_UI_ONLY()) && !r->GetRenderWindow()->GetStereoRender();
 
   r->GetBackground(bgColor);
 
